{
  "name": "cockchafer",
  "_about": "The cockchafer or May bug (Melolontha melolontha), 2.8 cm long: a stout cylinder -- black head and pronotum furred with grey hair, chestnut wing cases with four faint ribs and a white bloom, the white triangles down each side of the abdomen showing below them, the pointed pygidium sticking out behind; the male's antennae end in a fan of seven reddish leaves; reddish-brown legs, the front tibiae three-toothed. Coat: the red-necked form (a reddish pronotum). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/insects/beetles.py on insectlib.py (six jointed legs on a tripod gait, the antennae on bones of their own that wave).",
